      "name": "Latest Badge",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "latest-badge",
      "description": "Visual sample of the labeled first-session-record marker.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-latest\">Latest</span>",
      "css": ".ds-latest{display:inline-block;padding:3px 10px;border-radius:12px;background:#EFE1CD;color:#755026;font:600 12px/17px system-ui}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.ds-latest{background:#453526;color:#E1BC84}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Event Record",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "event-record",
      "description": "Interactive browser disclosure is a sample of the native inline payload structure; values are illustrative.",
      "html": "<details class=\"ds-event\"><summary><span class=\"ds-event-heading\"><strong>New block</strong><span>8m ago</span></span><span class=\"ds-event-latest\">Latest</span><span class=\"ds-event-body\">A new block was added to the chain.</span><span class=\"ds-event-show\">View event data <svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m4 6 4 4 4-4\"/></svg></span><span class=\"ds-event-hide\">Hide event data</span></summary><div class=\"ds-event-data\"><span>event_id</span><code>example-event-01</code><span>network</span><code>example-network</code></div></details>",
      "css": ".ds-event{background:#FFFFFF;color:#2F241C;border-radius:22px;overflow:hidden;font-family:system-ui}.ds-event summary{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;padding:18px 20px;list-style:none;cursor:pointer}.ds-event summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.ds-event summary:hover,.ds-event summary:active{opacity:.72}.ds-event summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #713F25;outline-offset:-3px}.ds-event-heading{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px}.ds-event-heading strong{font-size:18px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.3px}.ds-event-heading>span,.ds-event-data>span{font-size:12px;line-height:17px;color:#6D5B4C}.ds-event-latest{align-self:flex-start;border-radius:12px;background:#EFE1CD;color:#755026;padding:3px 10px;font:600 12px/17px system-ui}.ds-event-body{font-size:17px;line-height:25px;color:#6D5B4C}.ds-event-show,.ds-event-hide{color:#713F25;font-size:13px;line-height:19px;font-weight:600}.ds-event-show svg{vertical-align:middle}.ds-event-hide{display:none}.ds-event[open] .ds-event-show{display:none}.ds-event[open] .ds-event-hide{display:block}.ds-event-data{display:grid;gap:4px;padding:0 20px 18px;animation:ds-event-fade 180ms}.ds-event-data code{font:13px Menlo,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere;margin-bottom:8px}@keyframes ds-event-fade{from{opacity:.4}to{opacity:1}}@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.ds-event-data{animation:none}}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.ds-event{background:#2B221B;color:#F5EDE1}.ds-event-heading>span,.ds-event-body,.ds-event-data>span{color:#C7B5A2}.ds-event-latest{background:#453526;color:#E1BC84}.ds-event-show,.ds-event-hide{color:#D0A16D}.ds-event summary:focus-visible{outline-color:#D0A16D}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Settings Group",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "settings-group",
      "description": "Visual sample; browser Copy has no clipboard behavior.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-settings\"><div class=\"ds-settings-row\"><span>Notifications</span><span class=\"ds-settings-muted\">Allowed</span></div><div class=\"ds-settings-token\"><span>Push token</span><div><code>example123\u2026456abc</code><button>Copy</button></div></div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-settings{background:#FFFFFF;border-radius:22px;color:#2F241C;font:17px/25px system-ui;overflow:hidden}.ds-settings-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:18px}.ds-settings-row>span:first-child{flex-grow:1}.ds-settings-muted{color:#6D5B4C}.ds-settings-token{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;padding:18px}.ds-settings-token>div{display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center}.ds-settings-token code{flex:1;font:13px Menlo,monospace;color:#6D5B4C;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.ds-settings-token button{min-width:48px;min-height:48px;border:0;padding:0;background:transparent;color:#713F25;font:600 17px/25px system-ui;cursor:pointer}.ds-settings-token button:hover,.ds-settings-token button:active{opacity:.65}.ds-settings-token button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #713F25}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.ds-settings{background:#2B221B;color:#F5EDE1}.ds-settings-muted,.ds-settings-token code{color:#C7B5A2}.ds-settings-token button{color:#D0A16D}.ds-settings-token button:focus-visible{outline-color:#D0A16D}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Floating Glass Navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "tab-bar",
      "description": "Browser visual sample of the floating native glass pill. Backdrop blur approximates native GlassView/BlurView; sample attributes expose opaque fallback. SVG icons approximate platform symbols.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-tabs\" aria-label=\"Adder\"><button aria-current=\"page\"><span><svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.7\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M8 6h13M8 12h13M8 18h13\"/><circle cx=\"3\" cy=\"6\" r=\".6\"/><circle cx=\"3\" cy=\"12\" r=\".6\"/><circle cx=\"3\" cy=\"18\" r=\".6\"/></svg></span>Feed</button><button><span><svg width=\"22\" height=\"22\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.7\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"8\"/><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"3\"/><path d=\"M12 1v3M12 20v3M1 12h3M20 12h3M4 4l2 2M18 18l2 2M4 20l2-2M18 6l2-2\"/></svg></span>Settings</button></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-tabs{display:flex;gap:6px;padding:6px;width:100%;max-width:360px;border-radius:36px;background:rgba(244,239,231,.72);backdrop-filter:blur(18px);-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(18px);box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(39,26,16,.16)}.ds-tabs button{flex:1;min-height:60px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:3px;padding:7px 12px;border:0;border-radius:30px;background:transparent;color:#2F241C;font:400 12px/17px system-ui;text-align:center;cursor:pointer}.ds-tabs button>span{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}.ds-tabs button[aria-current]{background:#713F25;color:#FFF9EE;font-weight:600}.ds-tabs button:hover,.ds-tabs button:active{opacity:.7}.ds-tabs button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #713F25;outline-offset:2px}.ds-tabs[data-opaque]{background:#FFFFFF;backdrop-filter:none;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none}@supports not (backdrop-filter:blur(1px)){.ds-tabs{background:#FFFFFF}}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.ds-tabs{background:rgba(43,34,27,.72);box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(39,26,16,.3)}.ds-tabs button{color:#F5EDE1}.ds-tabs button[aria-current]{background:#D0A16D;color:#271A10}.ds-tabs button:focus-visible{outline-color:#D0A16D}.ds-tabs[data-opaque]{background:#2B221B}@supports not (backdrop-filter:blur(1px)){.ds-tabs{background:#2B221B}}}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Scanner Status",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "scanner-status",
      "description": "Visual sample of scanner status; camera preview and permissions require native UI.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-scanner\"><h3>Point at the code</h3><p>Your adder instance shows a QR code with its endpoint. Line it up in the frame.</p></div>",
      "css": ".ds-scanner{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;padding:22px;border-radius:22px;background:#FFFFFF;color:#2F241C;font-family:system-ui}.ds-scanner h3{margin:0;font-size:20px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.3px}.ds-scanner p{margin:0;color:#6D5B4C;font-size:17px;line-height:25px}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){.ds-scanner{background:#2B221B;color:#F5EDE1}.ds-scanner p{color:#C7B5A2}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Rounded Inbox",
    "overview": "Adder uses cream ground, white cards, deep brown text, and contrasting brown actions to make pairing and incoming events easy to read on a phone. The brown, tan, and cream palette comes from the existing Adder icon. Rounded surfaces and generous spacing establish a calm, mature mobile interface. Floating glass navigation adds the depth explicitly requested by the user. The name and app icon preserve Adder identity; working screens use text and platform symbols.\n\nThe user retained the clean, rounded direction, explicitly rejected divider-heavy presentation and pastels, and selected brown and beige with stronger contrast for an enterprise, App Store quality interface. This document records the implemented system in `src/theme.ts`, shared components, and the three screens. Frontmatter `px` values serialize React Native logical units; native text scales with system settings. Light/dark suffixes map to theme appearances and camera tokens are shared.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Cream ground, white cards, and contrasting brown actions.",
      "Rounded cards and controls with spacing between groups.",
      "Native typography, platform symbols, safe areas, and scalable content.",
      "Inline disclosure for complete selectable event data.",
      "A labeled amber Latest badge and floating glass navigation with filled selected tabs on both platforms."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Space Between Rule",
        "body": "Separate cards and settings groups with spacing and tonal surfaces. Keep screen dividers, timeline rails, and decorative outlines absent; camera corner guides remain functional.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Native Reading Rule",
        "body": "Preserve native text scaling, allow prose and data to wrap, and keep counts and timestamps subordinate to event content.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Shared Shape Rule",
        "body": "Use the card and control radii for their respective surfaces and the selected tab capsule on both iOS and Android.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do pair light and dark palette roles when adding a surface.",
      "Do separate groups with spacing and soft surface fills.",
      "Do use Adder brown/tan for actions, amber for the labeled Latest badge, and brick/coral for errors or unlinking.",
      "Do preserve native text scaling, wrapping, safe areas, touch targets, and Reduce Motion.",
      "Do expose complete event payloads as readable, selectable values.",
      "Do preserve the Adder name and existing app icon."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't add divider lines, timeline rails, decorative outlines, or card shadows; reserve glass and shadow for the floating navigation.",
      "Don't place mascot illustrations in Feed, Settings, or scanner screens.",
      "Don't remove the selected tab capsule from either platform.",
      "Don't label a linked endpoint healthy or live without a measured health signal.",
      "Don't treat fixture captures or JavaScript exports as proof of Android native appearance, physical QR pairing, or push delivery."
    ]
  }
}
